 <section class="lp-section" id="copy-opener"><div class="lp-wrap ctl-watch-grid">
  <div class="ctl-script"><p class="lp-kicker">Say it out loud</p><h2>Copy the opening exchange</h2><div id="opener-words"><p><b>Alex:</b> Hi Sam, Alex at CallTeam. When there is a company you would like to win, who makes the first call?</p><p><b>Buyer:</b> Our reps do.</p><p><b>Alex:</b> When they are busy closing deals, do they still get through that list?</p></div>{{ copy("opener-words", "Copy the opening exchange") }}<p>Replace Sam with your buyer’s name. Leave a pause after each question.</p><a class="lp-text-link" href="/resources/cold-call-scripts/#full-call">Read the full script and buyer replies →</a></div>
  <div><p class="lp-kicker">Use the answer to choose your next line</p><h2>Where to pause.<br>What to listen for.</h2><p><strong>When this opener fits:</strong> you provide outbound sales support and are calling a sales leader about accounts their team wants to win. For another offer, name a task that buyer actually owns.</p><ol class="ctl-steps"><li><strong>“Who makes the first call?” → Pause.</strong>Stop speaking after the question. Listen for who owns the outreach. If another person handles it, ask who you should speak with.</li><li><strong>“Our reps do.” → Ask about coverage.</strong>“When they are busy closing deals, do they still get through that list?” Pause again. Let the buyer tell you whether anything is being missed.</li><li><strong>“Some accounts get pushed back.” → Ask “Which ones?”</strong>A named account group gives the conversation a direction. If the buyer says the list is covered, thank them and finish the call.</li></ol><a class="lp-text-link" href="/articles/how-to-write-a-b2b-cold-call-script/">Write a script for your own offer →</a></div>
 </div></section>
